    <!-- Section 2 -->
    <section id="sec-2" class="lesson-section" style="border-top: 4px solid var(--adj-accent);">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2 class="section-title">2. TECHNICAL – The Adjective</h2>
        <span class="pos-pill pill-adj">Technical (adj.)</span>
      </div>

      <p>The word technical appeared in English in the 1610s.</p>
      <p>It was formed from technic + -al, and was also influenced by the Latin form of the Greek word tekhnikos.</p>
      <p>Its early meaning was:</p>
      <ul class="clean-list">
        <li>Having a particular skill or knowledge.</li>
        <li>Skilled in a particular art or subject.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Later, its meaning developed to describe things related to a particular profession, science or subject.</p>
      <p>Today, technical commonly means:</p>
      <ul class="clean-list recall-target">
        <li>Related to a particular subject, profession or type of work.</li>
        <li>Involving special knowledge or skills.</li>
      </ul>
      <span class="zh-definition recall-target" style="background:var(--adj-bg); color:var(--adj-text);">技術上的；專業的；與某個學科或行業有關的。</span>

      <h3>Examples</h3>
      <div class="examples-grid">
        <div class="example-card">
          <div class="example-num-title">1. Technical skills</div>
          <p class="example-en">You need good technical skills to repair computers.</p>
          <p class="example-zh recall-target">你需要良好的技術才能維修電腦。</p>
        </div>
        <div class="example-card">
          <div class="example-num-title">2. Technical knowledge</div>
          <p class="example-en">The students need more technical knowledge to understand how the machine works.</p>
          <p class="example-zh recall-target">學生需要更多專業知識，才能理解這部機器如何運作。</p>
        </div>
        <div class="example-card">
          <div class="example-num-title">3. Technical problem</div>
          <p class="example-en">The online meeting was cancelled because of a technical problem.</p>
          <p class="example-zh recall-target">網上會議因為技術問題而取消。</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="remember-box" style="background:var(--adj-bg); border-color:var(--adj-accent);">
        <div class="remember-box-title" style="color:var(--adj-text);">Remember:</div>
        <p style="margin:0;"><span class="recall-target">Technical describes something that requires or relates to special knowledge or skills.</span></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 3 -->
    <section id="sec-3" class="lesson-section" style="border-top: 4px solid var(--noun-tech-accent);">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2 class="section-title">3. TECHNIQUE – The Noun</h2>
        <span class="pos-pill pill-noun-tech">Technique (n.)</span>
      </div>

      <p>Now let's look at another word from the same word family.</p>
      <p>This word entered English in 1817 from French technique.</p>
      <p>The French word was connected to the Greek tekhnikos, which came from tekhnē.</p>
      <p>Its original meaning was related to the practical details of creating art or music.</p>
      <p>Over time, its meaning became broader.</p>
      <p>Today, it means:</p>
      <ul class="clean-list recall-target">
        <li>A particular way of doing something.</li>
        <li>A special method or skill used to complete a task.</li>
      </ul>
      <span class="zh-definition recall-target" style="background:var(--noun-tech-bg); color:var(--noun-tech-text);">技巧；技術；方法。</span>

      <p>Let's understand the difference between skill and technique.</p>
      <p>Imagine two students are learning how to play the piano.</p>
      <ul class="clean-list">
        <li>One student has good piano skills.</li>
        <li>The other student uses a special way of moving their fingers to play difficult music.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The special way of moving their fingers is called a technique.</p>
      <p>In simple words:</p>
      <p><strong><span class="recall-target">Technique = A particular method or way of doing something well.</span></strong></p>

      <h3>Examples</h3>
      <div class="examples-grid">
        <div class="example-card">
          <div class="example-num-title">1. Swimming technique</div>
          <p class="example-en">The coach taught the students a new swimming technique.</p>
          <p class="example-zh recall-target">教練教學生一種新的游泳技巧。</p>
        </div>
        <div class="example-card">
          <div class="example-num-title">2. Painting technique</div>
          <p class="example-en">This artist uses a special painting technique.</p>
          <p class="example-zh recall-target">這位藝術家使用一種特別的繪畫技巧。</p>
        </div>
        <div class="example-card">
          <div class="example-num-title">3. Study technique</div>
          <p class="example-en">Everyone has a different study technique.</p>
          <p class="example-zh recall-target">每個人都有不同的學習方法。</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="remember-box" style="background:var(--noun-tech-bg); border-color:var(--noun-tech-accent);">
        <div class="remember-box-title" style="color:var(--noun-tech-text);">Remember:</div>
        <p style="margin:0;"><span class="recall-target">Technique is a noun. It refers to the method or skill used to do something.</span></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 4 -->
    <section id="sec-4" class="lesson-section" style="border-top: 4px solid var(--noun-person-accent);">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2 class="section-title">4. TECHNICIAN – The Noun</h2>
        <span class="pos-pill pill-noun-person">Technician (n.)</span>
      </div>

      <p>Now let's look at a word that describes a person.</p>
      <p>This word appeared in English in 1833.</p>
      <p>It was formed from:</p>
      <div class="formula-box" style="background:var(--noun-person-bg); color:var(--noun-person-text); border:1px solid var(--noun-person-border);">Technic + -ian</div>
      <p>The suffix -ian is often used to describe a person who has a particular job, skill or area of knowledge.</p>
      <p>For example:</p>

      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Word</th>
              <th>Meaning</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Musician</strong></td>
              <td><span class="recall-target">A person who plays or creates music</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Historian</strong></td>
              <td><span class="recall-target">A person who studies history</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Technician</strong></td>
              <td><span class="recall-target">A person who has special technical skills</span></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p>Originally, technician referred to someone who was an expert in the technical details of a subject.</p>
      <p>By 1939, it was also commonly used to describe someone skilled in practical or mechanical work.</p>
      <p>Today:</p>
      <p><strong>Technician (n.) = <span class="recall-target">A person who has special technical skills and knowledge, especially someone who works with machines or equipment.</span></strong></p>
      <span class="zh-definition recall-target" style="background:var(--noun-person-bg); color:var(--noun-person-text);">技術人員；技師。</span>

      <h3>Examples</h3>
      <div class="examples-grid">
        <div class="example-card">
          <div class="example-num-title">1. Computer technician</div>
          <p class="example-en">The computer technician helped me repair my laptop.</p>
          <p class="example-zh recall-target">電腦技術人員幫我維修手提電腦。</p>
        </div>
        <div class="example-card">
          <div class="example-num-title">2. Laboratory technician</div>
          <p class="example-en">The laboratory technician checked the samples carefully.</p>
          <p class="example-zh recall-target">實驗室技術人員仔細檢查了樣本。</p>
        </div>
        <div class="example-card">
          <div class="example-num-title">3. Electrical technician</div>
          <p class="example-en">We called an electrical technician to fix the broken machine.</p>
          <p class="example-zh recall-target">我們請了一位電機技術人員來修理故障的機器。</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="remember-box" style="background:var(--noun-person-bg); border-color:var(--noun-person-accent);">
        <div class="remember-box-title" style="color:var(--noun-person-text);">Remember:</div>
        <p style="margin:0;"><span class="recall-target">Technician = A person who has special technical skills.</span></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Section 5 -->
    <section id="sec-5" class="lesson-section" style="border-top: 4px solid var(--adv-accent);">
      <div class="section-header">
        <h2 class="section-title">5. TECHNICALLY – The Adverb</h2>
        <span class="pos-pill pill-adv">Technically (adv.)</span>
      </div>

      <p>Now we have reached the word you originally wanted to learn!</p>
      <p>This word is formed by:</p>
      <div class="formula-box" style="background:var(--adv-bg); color:var(--adv-text); border:1px solid var(--adv-border);">TECHNICAL + -LY = TECHNICALLY</div>
      <p>The suffix -ly is commonly added to adjectives to form adverbs.</p>
      <p>Its meaning is:</p>
      <ul class="clean-list recall-target">
        <li>In a technical manner.</li>
        <li>According to the exact rules or meaning of a particular subject or profession.</li>
      </ul>
      <span class="zh-definition recall-target" style="background:var(--adv-bg); color:var(--adv-text);">技術上；嚴格來說；按照專業定義。</span>

      <div class="examples-grid">
        <div class="example-card">
          <div class="example-num-title">Meaning 1: In a technical manner</div>
          <p>It describes how something is done using special knowledge or skills.</p>
          <p class="example-en"><strong>Example:</strong><br>The machine was technically designed to work in extreme temperatures.</p>
          <p class="example-zh recall-target">這部機器在技術設計上能夠在極端溫度下運作。</p>
        </div>
        <div class="example-card">
          <div class="example-num-title">Meaning 2: According to the exact rules or facts</div>
          <p>Sometimes, technically is used when something is correct according to the rules or exact meaning of a word, even if people might understand it differently in everyday life.</p>
          <p class="example-en"><strong>Example:</strong><br>Technically, a tomato is a fruit, not a vegetable.</p>
          <p class="example-zh recall-target">嚴格來說，番茄是水果，而不是蔬菜。</p>
          <p style="margin-top:0.5rem;"><strong>Why?</strong><br>Because according to its botanical classification, a tomato is a fruit.<br>However, people often treat it as a vegetable when cooking.<br>This is why we use technically here: we are talking about what is correct according to a specific definition.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="remember-box" style="background:var(--adv-bg); border-color:var(--adv-accent);">
        <div class="remember-box-title" style="color:var(--adv-text);">Remember:</div>
        <p style="margin:0;"><span class="recall-target">Technically = According to the exact rules, facts or professional meaning of something.</span></p>
      </div>
    </section>

